[decoded] "Based on your repeated notes, here is a summary of how the hybrid model processes a token:\n\n*   **GatedDeltaNet Layer (Recurrent State):** Instead of maintaining a full key-value cache, this layer maintains a recurrent state per value head that decays by a learned factor at every position. The key retrieves the state's prediction, and the difference between the current value and that prediction (scaled by a learned rate) is written back as a rank-one update. The query then reads this updated state to generate the output.\n*   **Full Attention Layer (Classic Cache):** Three GatedDeltaNet layers alternate with one full attention layer. This layer maintains a classic cache of keys and values and attends over every earlier position using a partial rotary embedding applied to a quarter of each head.\n*   **Context Growth:** The **full attention layer** is the only component whose cache size grows with the length of the context, as it attends over every earlier position in the sequence"
